/-! # Self-extensions of a finite-dimensional module over a group algebra

Let `k` be a field, `Γ` a group and `M` a module over the group algebra `k[Γ]` which is finite
dimensional over `k` — that is, a finite-dimensional representation of `Γ`. If `Γ` is finitely
generated then the extension group `Ext¹_{k[Γ]}(M, N)` is finite dimensional over `k` for every
`N` which is finite dimensional over `k`.

The point is that this holds with no finiteness hypothesis whatsoever on the ring `k[Γ]`: the
group algebra of a free group on two generators is not Noetherian, has infinite global
dimension, and `Ext` over it is not finite in general. What makes the first extension group
finite is a *presentation with finitely generated relations*, which a finitely generated group
supplies:

* choose a `k`-basis `e_1, …, e_d` of `M` and let `π : k[Γ]^d → M` be the `k[Γ]`-linear map
  sending the `i`-th standard generator to `e_i`; it is surjective because the `e_i` already
  span `M` over `k`;
* let `σ : M → k[Γ]^d` be the `k`-linear — *not* `k[Γ]`-linear — section reading off basis
  coordinates;
* then the relation module `ker π` is generated, as a `k[Γ]`-module, by the `n · d` elements
  `γ_j · σ(e_i) - σ(γ_j · e_i)` for `γ_1, …, γ_n` a generating set of `Γ`.

That last statement is the cocycle-on-generators bound in disguise: `γ ↦ γ · σ(m) - σ(γ · m)`
is a `1`-cocycle in disguise, and a cocycle is determined by its values on generators. The
proof is an induction over `Subgroup.closure`, whose inverse step is the identity
`γ⁻¹ · σ(m) - σ(γ⁻¹ · m) = γ⁻¹ · (−(γ · σ(γ⁻¹ · m) - σ(m)))`.

Finitely many generators of `ker π` make `Hom_{k[Γ]}(ker π, N)` embed `k`-linearly into `N^{nd}`
and hence finite dimensional, and `Ext¹(M, N)` is a quotient of it by
`CategoryTheory.Abelian.Ext.finite_extOne_of_shortExact_of_projective`, since `k[Γ]^d` is free
and so projective.

## Main definitions

* `MonoidAlgebra.presentationMap`: the `k[Γ]`-linear surjection from a free module of rank
  `dim_k M` onto `M` determined by a `k`-basis of `M`.
* `MonoidAlgebra.presentationSection`: its `k`-linear section.
* `MonoidAlgebra.relationGen`: the `n · d` generators of the relation module.

## Main results

* `MonoidAlgebra.ker_presentationMap_eq_span`: the relation module of the presentation is
  generated by `MonoidAlgebra.relationGen`.
* `MonoidAlgebra.finite_extOne_of_basis`: `Ext¹_{k[Γ]}(M, N)` is finite dimensional over `k`,
  given a `k`-basis of `M`, a `k[Γ]`-basis of a free module of the same rank, and a finite
  generating set of `Γ`.
* `MonoidAlgebra.finite_extOne`: the same conclusion from `Group.FG Γ` and
  finite-dimensionality of `M` and `N` alone, the free module being constructed internally.

## Implementation notes

The `k`-module structure on a `k[Γ]`-module is the restriction of scalars along
`algebraMap k k[Γ]`, which for a bundled object of `ModuleCat k[Γ]` is
`ModuleCat.moduleOfAlgebraModule`; it and the compatibility `ModuleCat.isScalarTower_of_algebra`
are activated as local instances here, and a consumer must activate them too in order for
`Module.Finite k M` to mean the same thing. They are what the global instance
`ModuleCat.linearOverField : Linear k (ModuleCat k[Γ])` is built from, so the `k`-module
structure on the extension groups is the matching one.

`MonoidAlgebra.finite_extOne` needs a free `k[Γ]`-module in the universe of `M`, which exists
only when `k[Γ]` is small in that universe; that hypothesis is carried as `Small.{q} k[Γ]`.
It is not a restriction in practice — a nonzero `k`-vector space in `Type q` forces `k` to be
small in `Type q`, and a finitely generated group is countable — but it cannot be removed,
since over a genuinely larger ring the only module in `Type q` is zero and no free presentation
exists.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory MonoidAlgebra

attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.moduleOfAlgebraModule
  ModuleCat.isScalarTower_of_algebra_moduleCat

universe uR uF w g q t

/-- A `k[Γ]`-linear map out of a submodule is determined by its values on a generating set of
that submodule: the preimages in the submodule of a generating set of it span everything. -/
theorem Submodule.span_subtype_eq_top {R : Type uR} [Ring R] {F : Type uF} [AddCommGroup F]
    [Module R F] (K : Submodule R F) (s : Set F) (hs : Submodule.span R s = K)
    (hsub : s ⊆ (K : Set F)) :
    Submodule.span R {x : K | (x : F) ∈ s} = ⊤ := by
  have himg : K.subtype '' {x : K | (x : F) ∈ s} = s := by
    ext y
    simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Submodule.coe_subtype]
    exact ⟨fun ⟨_, hx, h⟩ ↦ h ▸ hx, fun hy ↦ ⟨⟨y, hsub hy⟩, hy, rfl⟩⟩
  apply Submodule.map_injective_of_injective K.injective_subtype
  rw [K.map_subtype_top, Submodule.map_span, himg, hs]

namespace MonoidAlgebra

variable {k : Type w} [Field k] {Γ : Type g} [Group Γ]
  {M F N : ModuleCat.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ)} {d : ℕ}
  (b : Module.Basis (Fin d) k M) (e : Module.Basis (Fin d) (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) F)

/-- The `k[Γ]`-linear map from a free module of rank `d` onto a `k[Γ]`-module with a `k`-basis
of size `d`, carrying the `i`-th basis vector of the free module to the `i`-th basis vector of
the target. It is surjective, so it presents the target. -/
def presentationMap : F →ₗ[MonoidAlgebra k Γ] M := e.constr k fun i ↦ b i

/-- The `k`-linear section of `MonoidAlgebra.presentationMap` reading off the coordinates of a
vector in the chosen `k`-basis. It is a section of a `k[Γ]`-linear map which is itself only
`k`-linear; the failure of its `k[Γ]`-linearity is exactly the cocycle whose values on a
generating set of the group generate the relation module. -/
def presentationSection : M →ₗ[k] F := b.constr k fun i ↦ e i

/-- `MonoidAlgebra.presentationSection` carries the `i`-th vector of the `k`-basis of the source
to the `i`-th vector of the basis of the free module. -/
theorem presentationSection_basis (i : Fin d) : presentationSection b e (b i) = e i := by
  simp [presentationSection]

/-- `MonoidAlgebra.presentationMap` carries the `i`-th vector of the basis of the free module to
the `i`-th vector of the `k`-basis of the target. -/
theorem presentationMap_basis (i : Fin d) : presentationMap b e (e i) = b i := by
  simp [presentationMap]

/-- `MonoidAlgebra.presentationSection` is a `k`-linear right inverse of
`MonoidAlgebra.presentationMap`. -/
theorem presentationMap_comp_section :
    ((presentationMap b e).restrictScalars k).comp (presentationSection b e) =
      LinearMap.id :=
  b.ext fun i ↦ by simp [presentationSection_basis, presentationMap_basis]

/-- `MonoidAlgebra.presentationMap` sends `MonoidAlgebra.presentationSection b e m` back to `m`. -/
theorem presentationMap_section (m : M) :
    presentationMap b e (presentationSection b e m) = m :=
  LinearMap.congr_fun (presentationMap_comp_section b e) m

/-- `MonoidAlgebra.presentationMap` is surjective. -/
theorem presentationMap_surjective : Function.Surjective (presentationMap b e) := by
  rw [← LinearMap.range_eq_top]
  have h : (LinearMap.range (presentationMap b e)).restrictScalars k = ⊤ := by
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← b.span_eq, Submodule.span_le]
    rintro x ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨e i, presentationMap_basis b e i⟩
  simpa using h

variable (gens : Finset Γ)

/-- The relation `γ · σ(e_i) - σ(γ · e_i)` of the presentation, indexed by a generator `γ` of
the group and a basis vector `e_i`; as the group acts on the chosen section only up to this
discrepancy, these elements lie in the kernel of the presentation, and
`MonoidAlgebra.ker_presentationMap_eq_span` says they generate it. -/
def relationGen (p : gens × Fin d) : LinearMap.ker (presentationMap b e) :=
  ⟨of k Γ (p.1 : Γ) • e p.2 - presentationSection b e (of k Γ (p.1 : Γ) • b p.2), by
    simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker, map_sub, map_smul, presentationMap_basis,
      presentationMap_section, sub_self]⟩

/-- The set of relations of the presentation, as a subset of the free module. -/
def relationSubset : Set F := Set.range fun p ↦ ((relationGen b e gens p : F))

/-- The relations of the presentation lie in the kernel of `MonoidAlgebra.presentationMap`. -/
theorem relationSubset_subset_ker :
    relationSubset b e gens ⊆ (LinearMap.ker (presentationMap b e) : Set F) :=
  Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun p ↦ (relationGen b e gens p).2

/-- The discrepancy `m ↦ γ · σ(m) - σ(γ · m)` by which the chosen `k`-linear section of the
presentation fails to be equivariant for a group element `γ`. It is `k`-linear in `m`, and as a
function of `γ` it is a `1`-cocycle with values in the maps `M → ker π`. -/
def sectionDiscrepancy (γ : Γ) : M →ₗ[k] F where
  toFun m := of k Γ γ • presentationSection b e m - presentationSection b e (of k Γ γ • m)
  map_add' x y := by
    simp only [map_add, smul_add]
    abel
  map_smul' a m := by
    simp only [map_smul, RingHom.id_apply, smul_sub]
    rw [smul_comm (of k Γ γ) a (presentationSection b e m), smul_comm (of k Γ γ) a m, map_smul]

/-- The value of `MonoidAlgebra.sectionDiscrepancy` at a group element `γ` on the `i`-th basis
vector `e_i` is `γ · σ(e_i) - σ(γ · e_i)`. -/
theorem sectionDiscrepancy_basis (γ : Γ) (i : Fin d) :
    sectionDiscrepancy b e γ (b i) =
      of k Γ γ • e i - presentationSection b e (of k Γ γ • b i) := by
  simp [sectionDiscrepancy, presentationSection_basis]

/-- **A cocycle is determined by its values on generators.** For every group element `γ` and
every vector `m`, the discrepancy `γ · σ(m) - σ(γ · m)` lies in the span of the finitely many
relations attached to a generating set of the group.

The induction is over `Subgroup.closure`: the `k`-linearity of the discrepancy in `m` reduces
each step to basis vectors, the multiplicative step is the cocycle identity
`c(γδ) = γ · c(δ) + c(γ)|_{δ · m}`, and the inverse step follows by applying `γ⁻¹` to the
multiplicative step at `γ` and `γ⁻¹ · m`. -/
theorem sectionDiscrepancy_mem_span (hgens : Subgroup.closure (gens : Set Γ) = ⊤) (γ : Γ)
    (m : M) :
    sectionDiscrepancy b e γ m ∈
      Submodule.span (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (relationSubset b e gens) := by
  set N₀ := Submodule.span (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (relationSubset b e gens)
  have hγ : γ ∈ Subgroup.closure (gens : Set Γ) := by simp [hgens]
  induction hγ using Subgroup.closure_induction generalizing m with
  | mem x hx =>
    have hW : (⊤ : Submodule k M) ≤
        Submodule.comap (sectionDiscrepancy b e x) (N₀.restrictScalars k) := by
      rw [← b.span_eq, Submodule.span_le]
      rintro y ⟨i, rfl⟩
      refine Submodule.mem_comap.mpr ?_
      rw [sectionDiscrepancy_basis]
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨(⟨x, hx⟩, i), rfl⟩
    exact hW (Submodule.mem_top : m ∈ (⊤ : Submodule k M))
  | one =>
    have h1 : sectionDiscrepancy b e (1 : Γ) m = 0 := by
      simp only [sectionDiscrepancy, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk]
      rw [map_one, one_smul, one_smul, sub_self]
    rw [h1]
    exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | mul x y hx hy ihx ihy =>
    have hrw : sectionDiscrepancy b e (x * y) m =
        of k Γ x • sectionDiscrepancy b e y m + sectionDiscrepancy b e x (of k Γ y • m) := by
      simp only [sectionDiscrepancy, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, map_mul, mul_smul,
        smul_sub]
      abel
    rw [hrw]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (ihy m)) (ihx _)
  | inv x hx ihx =>
    have hz : of k Γ x • sectionDiscrepancy b e x⁻¹ m =
        -sectionDiscrepancy b e x (of k Γ x⁻¹ • m) := by
      simp only [sectionDiscrepancy, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, smul_sub, ← mul_smul,
        ← map_mul, mul_inv_cancel, map_one, one_smul]
      abel
    have hmemz : of k Γ x • sectionDiscrepancy b e x⁻¹ m ∈ N₀ := by
      rw [hz]
      exact Submodule.neg_mem _ (ihx _)
    have hback : of k Γ x⁻¹ • (of k Γ x • sectionDiscrepancy b e x⁻¹ m) =
        sectionDiscrepancy b e x⁻¹ m := by
      rw [← mul_smul, ← map_mul, inv_mul_cancel, map_one, one_smul]
    rw [← hback]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hmemz

/-- The discrepancy of the section against an arbitrary element of the group algebra, not just a
group element, still lies in the span of the relations: the discrepancy is additive in the
scalar and `k`-homogeneous, so this follows from `MonoidAlgebra.sectionDiscrepancy_mem_span` by
the decomposition of an element of a group algebra into a `k`-combination of group elements. -/
theorem smul_section_sub_mem (hgens : Subgroup.closure (gens : Set Γ) = ⊤)
    (c : MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (m : M) :
    c • presentationSection b e m - presentationSection b e (c • m) ∈
      Submodule.span (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (relationSubset b e gens) := by
  induction c using MonoidAlgebra.induction_on with
  | of γ => exact sectionDiscrepancy_mem_span b e gens hgens γ m
  | add x y hx hy =>
      have hrw : (x + y) • presentationSection b e m -
            presentationSection b e ((x + y) • m) =
          (x • presentationSection b e m - presentationSection b e (x • m)) +
            (y • presentationSection b e m - presentationSection b e (y • m)) := by
        simp only [add_smul, map_add]
        abel
      rw [hrw]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy
  | smul a x hx =>
      have hrw : (a • x) • presentationSection b e m -
            presentationSection b e ((a • x) • m) =
          a • (x • presentationSection b e m - presentationSection b e (x • m)) := by
        rw [smul_assoc, smul_assoc, map_smul, smul_sub]
      rw [hrw, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) a]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hx

/-- Every element of the free module agrees, modulo the relations, with the section of its
image: this is what makes the relations generate the whole relation module. -/
theorem sub_section_presentationMap_mem (hgens : Subgroup.closure (gens : Set Γ) = ⊤) (x : F) :
    x - presentationSection b e (presentationMap b e x) ∈
      Submodule.span (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (relationSubset b e gens) := by
  have hx : x ∈ Submodule.span (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (Set.range e) := by
    rw [e.span_eq]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hy
    simp [presentationMap_basis, presentationSection_basis]
  | zero => simp
  | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
    convert Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy using 1
    simp only [map_add]
    abel
  | smul c x _ hx =>
    convert Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_mem _ c hx)
      (smul_section_sub_mem b e gens hgens c (presentationMap b e x)) using 1
    simp only [map_smul, smul_sub]
    abel

/-- **The relation module of the presentation is finitely generated.** For a finitely generated
group, the kernel of the free presentation of a finite-dimensional representation is generated
by the `n · d` relations `γ_j · σ(e_i) - σ(γ_j · e_i)`. -/
theorem ker_presentationMap_eq_span (hgens : Subgroup.closure (gens : Set Γ) = ⊤) :
    LinearMap.ker (presentationMap b e) =
      Submodule.span (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (relationSubset b e gens) :=
  le_antisymm (fun x hx ↦ by
      simpa [LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hx] using sub_section_presentationMap_mem b e gens hgens x)
    (Submodule.span_le.2 (relationSubset_subset_ker b e gens))

/-- Maps out of the relation module into a finite-dimensional module form a finite-dimensional
space: such a map is determined by its values on the finitely many relations, so evaluation
there is an injective `k`-linear map into a finite product. -/
theorem finite_hom_ker_presentationMap (hgens : Subgroup.closure (gens : Set Γ) = ⊤)
    (hN : Module.Finite k N) :
    Module.Finite k
      ((ModuleCat.of (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (LinearMap.ker (presentationMap b e))) ⟶ N) := by
  have := hN
  have hspan : Submodule.span (MonoidAlgebra k Γ)
      {x : LinearMap.ker (presentationMap b e) | (x : F) ∈ relationSubset b e gens} = ⊤ :=
    Submodule.span_subtype_eq_top _ _
      (ker_presentationMap_eq_span b e gens hgens).symm (relationSubset_subset_ker b e gens)
  let ev : ((ModuleCat.of (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (LinearMap.ker (presentationMap b e))) ⟶ N) →ₗ[k]
      (gens × Fin d → N) :=
    { toFun := fun f p ↦ f.hom (relationGen b e gens p)
      map_add' := fun _ _ ↦ rfl
      map_smul' := fun _ _ ↦ rfl }
  have hinj : Function.Injective ev := by
    intro f g hfg
    apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
    refine LinearMap.ext_on hspan ?_
    rintro x ⟨p, hp⟩
    obtain rfl : x = relationGen b e gens p := Subtype.ext hp.symm
    exact congrFun hfg p
  exact Module.Finite.of_injective ev hinj

include b e gens in
/-- **Finiteness of the first self-extension group over a group algebra**, given a presentation.
If `M` has a `k`-basis of size `d`, `F` is a free `k[Γ]`-module of rank `d`, the group `Γ` is
generated by the finite set `gens`, and `N` is finite dimensional over `k`, then
`Ext¹_{k[Γ]}(M, N)` is finite dimensional over `k`. -/
theorem finite_extOne_of_basis [HasExt.{t} (ModuleCat.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ))]
    (hgens : Subgroup.closure (gens : Set Γ) = ⊤) (hN : Module.Finite k N) :
    Module.Finite k (Abelian.Ext.{t} M N 1) := by
  let S := (presentationMap b e).shortComplexKer
  have hS : S.ShortExact :=
    LinearMap.shortExact_shortComplexKer (presentationMap_surjective b e)
  have : CategoryTheory.Projective S.X₂ := ModuleCat.projective_of_free e
  have : Module.Finite k (S.X₁ ⟶ N) := finite_hom_ker_presentationMap b e gens hgens hN
  exact Abelian.Ext.finite_extOne_of_shortExact_of_projective (k := k) hS N

/-- The group algebra of a finitely generated group over a field is small in the universe of
any module over that field containing a nonzero vector.

This is what makes a free presentation of such a module available: a nonzero `k`-vector space
in `Type q` forces `k` itself to be small in `Type q`, a finitely generated group is a quotient
of a free group on a finite type and so small in every universe, and the group algebra injects
into the finitely supported functions from the group to the field. -/
theorem small_of_ne_zero [Group.FG Γ] {V : Type q} [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V] {v : V}
    (hv : v ≠ 0) : Small.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) := by
  have hk : Small.{q} k := small_of_injective (smul_left_injective k hv)
  have hΓ : Small.{q} Γ := by
    obtain ⟨α, hα, φ, hφ⟩ :=
      Group.fg_iff_exists_freeGroup_hom_surjective_finite.mp (inferInstance : Group.FG Γ)
    have : Finite α := hα
    exact small_of_surjective hφ
  exact small_of_injective (f := MonoidAlgebra.coeff) MonoidAlgebra.coeff_injective

/-- **Finiteness of the first self-extension group over a group algebra.** For a finitely
generated group `Γ` and two `k[Γ]`-modules which are finite dimensional over `k`, the first
extension group `Ext¹_{k[Γ]}(M, N)` is finite dimensional over `k`.

No finiteness assumption is made on `k[Γ]`, which is for instance not Noetherian when `Γ` is
free of rank two. The free presentation of `M` is built here from a `k`-basis of `M` and the
rank-one free module `Shrink k[Γ]`, which is where the smallness hypothesis is used; see the
implementation notes. That hypothesis is deliberately *not* an instance argument: making it one
lets `ModuleCat.instHasExt` fire at a call site and silently choose a different universe for the
extension group than the one `HasExt.standard` gives. -/
theorem finite_extOne [Group.FG Γ] (M N : ModuleCat.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ))
    [HasExt.{t} (ModuleCat.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ))]
    (hsmall : Small.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ))
    (hM : Module.Finite k M) (hN : Module.Finite k N) :
    Module.Finite k (Abelian.Ext.{t} M N 1) := by
  have := hsmall
  have := hM
  obtain ⟨-, gens, -, hgens⟩ := Group.fg_iff'.mp (inferInstance : Group.FG Γ)
  let d := Module.finrank k (M : Type q)
  let bM : Module.Basis (Fin d) k (M : Type q) := Module.finBasis k (M : Type q)
  let Fr : ModuleCat.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) :=
    ModuleCat.of (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (Fin d →₀ Shrink.{q} (MonoidAlgebra k Γ))
  let eF : Module.Basis (Fin d) (MonoidAlgebra k Γ) (Fr : Type q) :=
    Module.Basis.ofRepr (Finsupp.mapRange.linearEquiv (Shrink.linearEquiv _ _))
  exact finite_extOne_of_basis bM eF gens hgens hN

end MonoidAlgebra

end
